### P2P transfers (FR-P-1 to FR-P-3, M6). Fake test data only.
# Prerequisites: tokens for customer1, customer2 and officer1 from auth.http; both customers at FULL KYC
# (kyc.http), so both have FULL wallets. Run GET /wallets/me as customer2 first to capture its wallet ID.
# Top-ups arrive in M7: until then, fund customer1 for a manual run with a TOPUP posting + credit, or expect
# 422 INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS on the transfer below.

### customer2: own wallet (captures the recipient wallet ID)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/wallets/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2_token}}

> {% client.global.set("receiver_wallet_id", response.body.walletId); %}

### customer1 -> customer2 by wallet ID -> 201 {status COMPLETED, amount "250.00"}
# Change nothing and run again -> same 201 body with header Idempotent-Replayed: true, money moved once.
# Change the amount and run again with the same key -> 422 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED.
POST {{api}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Idempotency-Key: 6f1f8a52-2a8e-4b7e-9d43-3c0f6a1d2b01
Content-Type: application/json

{"recipientWalletId": "{{receiver_wallet_id}}", "amount": "250.00", "note": "Test dinner split"}

> {% client.global.set("transfer_id", response.body.id); %}

### Same transfer without Idempotency-Key -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{api}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"recipientWalletId": "{{receiver_wallet_id}}", "amount": "250.00"}

### At or above ₹50,000 -> 201 {status HELD_FOR_REVIEW}; the amount moves to "held" on GET /wallets/me
POST {{api}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Idempotency-Key: 6f1f8a52-2a8e-4b7e-9d43-3c0f6a1d2b02
Content-Type: application/json

{"recipientWalletId": "{{receiver_wallet_id}}", "amount": "50000.00"}

### Bad amount (3 decimals) -> 400
POST {{api}}/api/v1/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
Idempotency-Key: 6f1f8a52-2a8e-4b7e-9d43-3c0f6a1d2b03
Content-Type: application/json

{"recipientWalletId": "{{receiver_wallet_id}}", "amount": "10.001"}

### Sender reads it -> 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/transfers/{{transfer_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### Receiver reads it -> 200
GET {{api}}/api/v1/transfers/{{transfer_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2_token}}

### An officer on the customer endpoint -> 403
GET {{api}}/api/v1/transfers/{{transfer_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}
